  "content": "{\n  \"path\": \"docs/standards/ui-core.md\",\n  \"startLine\": 1,\n  \"endLine\": 187,\n  \"totalLines\": 187,\n  \"truncated\": false,\n  \"content\": \"1|# UI core — forms, shell, copy, feedback\\n2|\\n3|> **Shard:** `ui-core`  \\n4|> **Tokens:** [`ui-design-system.md`](./ui-design-system.md) — do not restate color/type/radius/elevation here.  \\n5|> **Controls:** Base Components `/studio/base-components` (always-on in `AGENTS.md`).\\n6|\\n7|## Intent\\n8|\\n9|How product forms, the admin shell, and feedback behave. Visual tokens are the design-system shard.\\n10|\\n11|## MUST\\n12|\\n13|- Use Base Components primitives (`UiInput`, `UiTextarea`, `UiCheckbox`, `UiRadioGroup`, `UiSelect`, `UiCombobox`, `FormField`, `FormSection`, `AppToast`, `FloatingPanelShell`, …).\\n14|- English-only strings in TS/TSX/JSON. Markdown docs exempt.\\n15|- Tenant entity labels: canonical English `label` on the record + seeded `settings.attributes.label.{key}` in Cultures → Translations. No `label_en` / `label_fa` columns. Resolve `t(key)` → `label` → `key`.\\n16|- Label over input: one vertical stack, label `ps-[4px]`, **2px** gap to control.\\n17|- Default control size `sm` (`heroFieldSize.ts`). One size per form surface.\\n18|- Required fields: invalid rose border **from first paint** until valid (`FormField` `invalid` / `required`). Overlay feedback default (`feedbackPlacement=\\\"overlay\\\"`). Overlay balloons prefer **above** the control and flip **below** when the viewport or a clipping ancestor has no room.\\n19|- Field hints: `FieldHintTooltip` / `FormField hint` — never under-field helper paragraphs or native `title=` for field guidance. The studio page guide reads the same `hint` (plus `title`) from `data-page-guide*` — see §Page guide.\\n20|- Shell loading: never a blank white viewport — `AppRouteLoading` (see below).\\n21|- In-shell menu/link clicks raise the embedded cover **from the click**, not after the URL commits. React may keep the previous page on screen until the next chunk is ready; `useShellNavigate` / `beginShellNavigationPending` must not wait for that. Same-path and CMS Settings soft-nav stay uncovered.\\n22|- Text `autoDir` on for `UiInput` / `UiTextarea` / Markdown editor except machine/identifier fields (`autoDir={false}`). Markdown editor `dir=\\\"auto\\\"` (default) uses the first meaningful character (`getContentTextDirection`); explicit `dir=ltr|rtl` wins.\\n23|\\n24|## NEVER\\n25|\\n26|- Raw `<input>` / `<textarea>` / `<select>` / native checkbox in product forms. Exceptions: `type=\\\"file\\\"|\\\"hidden\\\"|\\\"color\\\"` and designer runtime/export parity widgets.\\n27|- Hand-rolled HeroUI Radio/Checkbox rows — use `UiCheckboxChoiceList` / `UiRadioChoiceList` / `UiRadioGroup`. Exclusive **title + description** options use option cards (§ below) — do not add radio dots to those boxes.\\n28|- Large saturated panel or page color washes.\\n29|- `window.confirm` — [`ui-dialog.md`](./ui-dialog.md) §Danger.\\n30|- Ad-hoc HeroUI toasts — `showAppFeedbackToast` → `AppToastHost`.\\n31|\\n32|## Color it / رنگیش کن\\n33|\\n34|Tokens: design-system Tier 2/3. Recipe:\\n35|\\n36|1. Targets: small backgrounds, borders, fonts/labels, icons — never modal/page body fills.\\n37|2. Meaning first: identity indigo/violet, technical cyan, relation emerald/lime, caution/PK amber, danger rose, success emerald.\\n38|3. Reuse `FormSection` tones, `APP_SURFACE_BOX_TONE_CLASS`, `buttonSemantics.ts`.\\n39|4. Restraint: a few accents, not every element.\\n40|5. Named section lists (nav rails, group headers) keep **per-item hue visible at rest**.\\n41|\\n42|## Page guide\\n43|\\n44|The sidebar Bot companion walks `[data-page-guide]` stops that have both **title** and **hint**. **Page content first** (toolbars, create, grids, dialogs, designer, Data Studio). Shell header and sidebar chrome are **last**. Skip self-explanatory landing chrome (**Home** nav, studio logo). Play advances to the next stop every 8 seconds; pause or the last stop ends autoplay. While playing, a cyan circular countdown rings the play control. Click the companion to cycle body shapes. Drag it away and release — it hops back under the bubble. A CircleHelp control beside close in the bubble closes the tour and opens AppEndO chat — the companion leaves while the chat panel is open. The same CircleHelp beside close on the chat panel (and the sidebar trigger while chat is open) closes chat and brings the tour companion back. The active hotspot stays visible — the bubble and companion do not cover it. Hotspot dots swallow pointer events so the control underneath does not activate. Bubble controls are ghost icon-only (`ICON_ACTION_*`). Do not invent filler copy on every existing field or unlabeled nav item.\\n45|\\n46|How the guide learns a stop:\\n47|\\n48|- `FormField` `hint` and `FormSection` `hint` or `description`\\n49|- `FieldHintTooltip`\\n50|- Settings `labelInfo`\\n51|- `PageHeaderToolbar` `description`\\n52|- Shared page primitives: `ToolbarSearchInput`, `ToolbarRefreshButton`, `GridPagingFooter`, `AppButton intent=\\\"create\\\"`, `AppSearchBox`, `ToolbarFilterRadioGroup`, `ToolbarFilterSelect`, `ToolbarFilterCheckbox`, `ToolbarFilterMatchLogicBadge`, `AppSplitButton intent=\\\"create\\\"`, dialog/wizard headers, floating panel titles\\n53|- `pageGuideProps({ title, hint, priority, scope: 'local' })` or `pageGuideLocalProps` / `pageGuideChromeProps` / `pageGuideNavItemProps`\\n54|- Designer/CRUD generators: field `hint` on the node (runtime + exported TSX wrap the control)\\n55|\\n56|**IDs:** `ui.page-guide.hints`\\n57|\\n58|## Forms\\n59|\\n60|Canonical: Base Components → Form fields group (`text-fields`, `choice-fields`, `selection-fields`, `structured-fields`, `ai-fields`, `ai-chat-panel`).\\n61|\\n62|- Group with flat `FormSection` + `FormField` — §Form sections below. Intra-stack `flex flex-col gap-1`.\\n63|- **Do not** wrap ordinary fields in bordered panel boxes. Boxed shells are for **choice lists**, **option cards**, and **data hosts** (grids) only.\\n64|- Pair short fields: `resolveFormFieldPairGridClass(true)`. Full-width (textarea) below the pair grid.\\n65|- `FormField layout=\\\"side\\\"` (dense inspectors / dialog title bands): label column and control share **one horizontal midline** (`items-center`, `FORM_FIELD_SIDE_LABEL_COLUMN_CLASS`). Do not `items-start` that row. Stack layout stays label-over-input (`gap-[2px]`, label `ps-[4px]`).\\n66|- Invalid border: `HEROUI_FIELD_INVALID_BORDER_CLASS` / `resolveHeroUiFieldBorderClass` — no per-page red borders.\\n67|- `ui_color`: picker + hex in one field container.\\n68|- Combobox vs autocomplete: typeable filterable pickers use `UiCombobox`, not button-style `UiAutocomplete`. `menuTrigger`: `focus` (default, open the list on focus) · `input` (suggestions only after typing) · `manual` (chevron only).\\n69|\\n70|### Form sections\\n71|\\n72|Gold sample: Portals → Edit portal (`PortalsPageView` + `PortalBrandFields`). Match that chrome; do not invent a parallel heading.\\n73|\\n74|`FormSection` owns the header: ink accent bar, CSS-uppercased eyebrow title, optional hint icon, optional ink wash. Callers pass **sentence-case English** titles (`Portal`, `Identity`, `Redirect`, `Layout`) — never pre-uppercased strings, never a raw `<h2>`/`<h3>` plus a handmade bar.\\n75|\\n76|**Write a section**\\n77|\\n78|1. One `FormSection` per conceptual group. Title is a short noun or noun phrase (1–2 words). Do not use a sentence or a field-name dump as the section title.\\n79|2. First group: omit `divided`. Every later group: `divided` (`FORM_SECTION_DIVIDED_CLASS` / `pt-3`). No extra `<hr>` or border-b between sections.\\n80|3. Outer body stack: `flex flex-col gap-1`. Intra-section field stack is the component default (`FORM_SECTION_BODY_STACK_CLASS` / `space-y-2`).\\n81|4. Section guidance uses `hint` (info icon after the title). On dense create/edit, do not also pass `description` (visible under-heading paragraph). Field guidance stays on `FormField hint`.\\n82|5. Two related short fields: `resolveFormFieldPairGridClass(true)`. Full-width controls (textarea, long copy) sit **below** the pair grid. A logo + stacked titles row may use a custom flex row inside the same section — still not a bordered panel.\\n83|6. `ink` is required on product create/edit (not `tone` palettes). Rotate channels so adjacent sections differ:\\n84|   - `accent` — primary record identity (Portal, Layout)\\n85|   - `complement` — related chrome / brand (Identity)\\n86|   - `contrast` — policy / routing (Redirect)\\n87|   Repeat a channel only after another channel sits between. Nested `FormField` labels inherit the section ink.\\n88|7. Dialog top bands (Enabled, System Protected) are **not** `FormSection`s. Keep them on the create/edit enabled band; do not wrap them as PORTAL / ENABLED groups.\\n89|\\n90|**Never**\\n91|\\n92|- Hand-rolled section headers, `uppercase` in the title string, or under-heading helper `<p className=\\\"text-[10px] …\\\">`.\\n93|- `rounded-md border` / `AppSurfaceBox` around a field group. **Exception:** read-only nested-editor inspector cards — [`ui-inspector-rail.md`](./ui-inspector-rail.md). Do not use `FormSection` ink bars on those rails.\\n94|- `tone` on product create/edit when `ink` is available (Settings / catalog config may still use `tone`).\\n95|- A `FormSection` with no fields (empty chrome).\\n96|\\n97|Settings config uses `SettingsFormGroup` instead — same divided/flat rules, different typography. Living catalog: Base Components → text-fields.\\n98|\\n99|**IDs:** `ui.form.section.write`, `ui.form.section.intra-stack`, `ui.form.flat-sections-no-boxes` (inspector cards: `ui.inspector-rail.*`), `ui.form.field.side-align`\\n100|\\n101|### Exclusive option cards\\n102|\\n103|When each exclusive option has a **title plus description** (mode / policy / encryption pickers — not a short label list):\\n104|\\n105|- One **button/box per option**. Layout via `UiOptionCardGroup` `columns` (2 → side-by-side, 3 → three-up, 1 → stacked).\\n106|- **No visible radio** — not `UiRadioChoiceList`, not a radio-card wrapper, not HeroUI `Radio`. Host `role=\\\"radiogroup\\\"`; each control `role=\\\"radio\\\"` + `aria-checked`.\\n107|- Selected state is **border + light fill** (`accentClassName`, or the option’s `tone` wash), not a filled disc.\\n108|- Optional Lucide icon sits **in the title row** (`inline-flex items-center gap-1.5`; icon `h-3.5 w-3.5` compact / `h-4 w-4` default) — never a separate chip beside the body.\\n109|- Optional per-option `tone` (`AppSurfaceBoxTone`) tints border, icon, and title **at rest**; selected adds the tone strip wash. Descriptions wrap to multiple lines (`whitespace-pre-line`). Group `accentClassName` is the fallback when an option has no `tone`.\\n110|- Field label stays above the grid (label-over-input, `gap-[2px]`).\\n111|- Two options → `columns={2}`. Three title+description options → `columns={3}`. Long stacked lists → `columns={1}`. Short name chips that hug their label → `columns=\\\"auto\\\"` (flex wrap, width fits the title).\\n112|- Living sample: `UiOptionCardGroup` (`src/shared/ui/UiOptionCardGroup.tsx`) — Base Components → Choice. Product wrapper: `SmtpEncryptionField` on Settings → Email / SMTP and the install email step.\\n113|\\n114|Short label-only exclusive lists still use `UiRadioChoiceList`.\\n115|\\n116|### Settings forms\\n117|\\n118|- `SettingsFormGroup` over `FormSection`. First group plain, later groups `divided`.\\n119|- Intra-group `SETTINGS_FORM_GROUP_BODY_STACK_CLASS`; grids `SETTINGS_FORM_GRID_GAP_CLASS`.\\n120|- Feature toggles **disable** dependent fields (`SettingsDisabledFieldset`) — do not unmount them.\\n121|- `labelInfo` sits immediately after the label; reserve the 16×16 slot (`reserveInfoSlot`).\\n122|- Stacked full-width fields: `labelBand={false}`.\\n123|- New field labels follow design-system **Field label**. Existing screens keep `getSettingsTypography()` until a migration pass.\\n124|\\n125|### WHERE builder\\n126|\\n127|Base Components → where-builder · `UiWhereBuilder`. Nested AND/OR on the **group header**. Field/operator = `UiSelectMenu`. Text values may pick `contextItems` (server context). Manual expression is one-way (delete to leave). `allowReorder` for sibling/group drag. Do not invent a parallel predicate editor.\\n128|\\n129|### EUA fields\\n130|\\n131|Base Components → AI assist. `AiAssistFormField` inside `AiFieldAssistSectionProvider`. Structured extract launcher in the form **header toolbar**, not `FormSection headerExtra`. Pair-grid: reserve sparkle slot on the plain neighbor (`AI_FIELD_LABEL_EXTRA_PLACEHOLDER_CLASS`).\\n132|\\n133|### AI chat panel\\n134|\\n135|Base Components → AI Chat Panel · `UiContextChatPanel`. One chrome for SQL Console, Image Editor, SSH Hub, File Hub, Server Functions editor, and the AppEndO header agent. Hosts send context and apply returned actions. Docking (beside a console vs inside a host window) is host layout — not a catalog option on this panel. Agency is host-settable (`agencyModes` / `agencyMode` / `agencyPickerVariant`): **Ask** replies in the panel only, **Read only** auto-runs read commands (SQL SELECT, SSH inspect), **Agentic** runs every suggested action. Picker chrome is header buttons or a dropdown next to the model. Omit `agencyModes` when the host owns a different mode control (AppEndO Ask/Agent/Plan). Do not rebuild message list / prompt / model / send chrome per surface — mount this panel and pass slots (`headerSlot`, `bodySlot`, `promptToolbarStart`, `promptComposerStart`, `onSend` or `onSubmitPrompt`). Session history (AppEndO) stays in the host window, not inside this panel. Code in assistant markdown and command cards uses `ChatCodeBlock`: hosts pass `codeDiffBaseline` so a full replacement shows **changed lines only** (not the whole file); dumps longer than five displayed lines collapse behind an `AppButton intent=\\\"utility\\\"` expand/collapse. Short snippets stay as code. Copy still copies the full source.\\n136|\\n137|## Responsive (selective)\\n138|\\n139|Desktop-first chrome, **all studio pages work on phone and tablet**. Stacked toolbars, `presentation=\\\"auto\\\"` grids, `CreateEditModalShell` near-fullscreen on phone **and tablet**. Do **not** set `minViewport: 'desktop'` on studio route nav or pageKeys — Server Functions, Git, Data Studio, File Manager, SSH/RDP/File Hub stay reachable below 1024px. Optional `minViewport` on a custom/published binding still hides that one nav item via `filterAdminShellNavByViewport` and renders `DesktopOnlyGate` on deep link. Studio chrome: phone and tablet (≤1023) hamburger overlay drawer — no docked rail and no hover flyouts (pointer hover is not a tablet/phone affordance); desktop ≥1024 expandable docked rail — do not change desktop ≥1024. Compact chrome keeps the AppEnd **mark-only** logo (`appendo-logo-only.png`) in the header and overlay drawer on phone and tablet (the sidebar lockup is off-canvas). Desktop ≥1024 keeps the full lockup (`appendo-logo.png`). Page guide hidden on phone, available on tablet+. Breakpoints: JS `viewportTokens` phone ≤399 / tablet 400–1023 / desktop ≥1024; Tailwind `md` 768 / `lg` 1024 / `xl` 1280. `useViewportTier()` + `isOverlayNavTier` + `isCompactChromeTier`. AppEndoo overlay (not dock) on phone and tablet.\\n140|\\n141|## Floating panels\\n142|\\n143|`FloatingPanelShell` / `ToolboxPanelShell`. Default `border-2` via `FLOATING_PANEL_SHELL_CHROME_BORDER_CLASS` + `resolveSurfaceChrome`. Body white; tint on border/header/footer only. Click raises z-stack. Modeler windows: [`data-studio-modeler.md`](./data-studio-modeler.md).\\n144|\\n145|## Canvas viewport\\n146|\\n147|Every pan/zoom canvas uses the same overlay layout. Three slots are fixed: **search** (`CanvasSearchBox` = `AppSearchBox`) at **top-left**; **zoom** in / out / fit (`CanvasViewportControls` / `CanvasFlowViewportControls`) at **bottom-left**; **layout** at **bottom-right** (above MiniMap when present). Every other canvas button (toolbox, execute, settings, …) sits at **top-right**. MiniMap stays bottom-right. Dotted slate background (`#cbd5e1`, 16px). The canvas **clips overflow** — no native scrollbars. Pan with pointer drag; wheel zooms. Do not invent a parallel zoom bar, percent label, or per-surface xyflow `Controls` styling. File-manager image preview stays its own compact inline zoom (not a canvas). **ID:** `ui.canvas.viewport-controls`\\n148|\\n149|## Overlay motion\\n150|\\n151|Menus, drawers, flyouts, popovers, and dialogs open with a directional enter that matches the **trigger edge**. Phone/tablet hamburger and start-edge drawers slide from `start` (RTL-aware). Desktop collapsed-rail flyouts emerge from the rail. Popovers and split-button menus grow from the placement edge against the trigger (`bottom-start` → origin `top-start`). Compact fullscreen dialogs rise from the bottom; desktop dialogs scale from center. AppEndoo overlay enters from the header end. Use `overlayMotionPanelProps` / `overlayMotionBackdropProps` in `src/shared/ui/overlay-motion/overlayMotion.ts` — do not invent ad-hoc fade/slide classes. Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.\\n152|\\n153|## Admin shell\\n154|\\n155|Page, sidebar, and header share one light tone. Content host flush right/bottom; start-edge lift shadow only. Shell header and sidebar default to **no** line-pattern texture (`header-line-pattern` / `menu-line-pattern` stay off the chrome class names). Theme Designer can raise `--app-menu-texture-opacity` / `--app-header-texture-opacity` and `--app-sidebar-fill-opacity` / `--app-header-fill-opacity` (0% default). Geometric atmosphere behind chrome is **on by default**; Theme Designer can turn `--app-atmosphere-geometry` off. **ID:** `ui.admin-shell.no-chrome-texture`\\n156|\\n157|Compact header (`<lg`): fixed **52px** content band, `items-center`. Each control’s center is equidistant from the header top and bottom. `env(safe-area-inset-top)` is **extra padding above** that band (notch), not a substitute for vertical padding — do not pair `py-1.5` with top-only `pt-[env(safe-area-inset-top)]`. Inner row is `h-full items-center`. Desktop `lg:h-[59px]` unchanged. **ID:** `ui.admin-shell.header-vertical-center`\\n158|\\n159|Below `sm` (640px) the first header row cannot hold hamburger + mark + title + actions. Hide the inline title and add a **second header band** (`ADMIN_SHELL_HEADER_TITLE_ROW_CLASS`) with the page title centered. Do not change `sm` through desktop. **ID:** `ui.admin-shell.header-title-row`\\n160|\\n161|Every client component inherits **`UiClientComponent`**. Default is **all sizes**: `minViewport` `always` + `belowMin` `continue`. Set `tablet` / `desktop` and `hide` / `placeholder` only for a named exception. `placeholder` is the Desktop only body message. Living sample: Base Components → Client component. Designer inspector exposes the same props on every node. **ID:** `ui.client-component.viewport-host`\\n162|\\n163|Profile drawer is an **end-edge overlay**, not a full-screen sheet. Never `w-full`. Cap at 400px and leave a page peek of the collapsed-rail width (`81px` / `--admin-shell-sidebar-width-collapsed`) so the shell stays visible and tappable to dismiss — same idea as the hamburger overlay. **ID:** `ui.admin-shell.profile-drawer-peek`\\n164|\\n165|## Shell loading (no blank white)\\n166|\\n167|- `AppRouteLoading` `variant=\\\"fullscreen\\\"` for boot/shell/auth. Same look as `#app-boot-splash`. Colors from **active accent** — never hardcoded teal.\\n168|- `variant=\\\"embedded\\\"` for lazy pages inside a mounted shell.\\n169|- In-shell nav: `useShellNavigate` marks pending on click so `ShellRouteEnter` covers the content host immediately (same embedded `AppRouteLoading`), then keeps the cover until formatted reveal. Do not wait for the route to commit. Same-path and CMS Settings soft-nav skip the cover.\\n170|- First paint: `#app-boot-splash` in `index.html` with theme CSS vars; hydrate `localStorage` `appendo-accent-css-v3` in `<head>`.\\n171|- Keep splash until `ShellFormattedReveal` `onRevealed`. Wrap chrome in `ShellChromeEnter`, outlet in `ShellRouteEnter`. Atmosphere lives **inside** the cover, not as a sibling.\\n172|- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.\\n173|\\n174|## Toasts\\n175|\\n176|Top center: `fixed top-4 left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2`. `AppToast` types `success | error | warning | info`. Success/info auto-dismiss (~2.6–4s). **Error toasts stay until the operator dismisses them** (X). `showAppFeedbackToast` uses `durationMs: 0` for errors.\\n177|\\n178|## Base Info icons\\n179|\\n180|Store `<i data-lucide=\\\"IconName\\\"></i>` in `ui_html`. Render `BaseInfoUiIcon`.\\n181|\\n182|## Tokens / files\\n183|\\n184|`heroFieldSize.ts` · `formChoiceLayout.ts` · `HeroFieldControls.tsx` · `surfaceClasses.ts` · `AppRouteLoading.tsx` · `AppToast.tsx` · `FloatingPanelShell.tsx` · `useShellNavigate.ts` · `shellNavigationPending.ts`\\n185|\\n186|**IDs:** `ui.base-components.first`, `ui.heroui.*`, `ui.component.default-size`, `ui.where-builder`, `ui.copy.english-only`, `ui.content.labels-via-cultures`, `ui.form.*` (field/settings/section), `ui.form.section.write`, `ui.page-guide.hints`, `ui.shell.loading-alive-surface`, `ui.admin-shell.*`, `ui.responsive.selective`, `ui.overlay.directional-motion`, `ui.floating-panel.border`, `ui.canvas.viewport-controls`, `ui.feedback.toast.*`, `data.base-info.ui-html.icon-format`.\\n187|\"\n}"
}